From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 23:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: input: samsung,s6sy761: Add the S6SY771

The S6SY771 speaks the same protocol and is driven by the same code, so it
belongs to this binding rather than to one of its own.  It differs in one
detail the driver has to know about, and a compatible of its own is how it
gets told.

Found on a Galaxy S10+, where the touchscreen answers a device ID read with
ac 37 71.
Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 .../bindings/input/touchscreen/samsung,s6sy761.yaml         | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/samsung,s6sy761.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/samsung,s6sy761.yaml
index 1ffd17af3c5..7e2b3a40821 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/samsung,s6sy761.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/samsung,s6sy761.yaml
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 $id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/input/touchscreen/samsung,s6sy761.yaml#
 $schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
 
-title: Samsung S6SY761 touchscreen controller
+title: Samsung S6SY761 and S6SY771 touchscreen controllers
 
 maintainers:
   - Andi Shyti <andi.shyti@kernel.org>
@@ -14,7 +14,9 @@ allOf:
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    const: samsung,s6sy761
+    enum:
+      - samsung,s6sy761
+      - samsung,s6sy771
 
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
